nodecode-agentstatus-index is a rewrite of Carmel-Labs-Inc's Carmel-Labs-Inc/agentstatus-mcp-index:

  https://github.com/Carmel-Labs-Inc/agentstatus-mcp-index
  commit 8678c389f76a928a530d868eb9f51ead14e02783
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Carmel Labs Inc. (LICENSE)

The original was a portable Agent Plugins v1 package with no code of its own: plugin.json, mcp.json declaring the hosted index at https://index.mcp.agentstatus.dev/mcp (Streamable HTTP, no key), and one skill, agentstatus-index, that taught a model the workflow. This rewrite speaks that server's MCP wire itself, in Common Lisp over nlk:http -- initialize, the Mcp-Session-Id, tools/list, tools/call, one JSON-RPC POST per call, an answer that is either a JSON object or a one-event stream -- and keeps the server's own tool names (search_records, recommend_records, get_record, compare_records, list_sections, call_indexed_tool) behind seven purpose-named tools, each call checked against the catalog the server itself lists. The skill's rules are the cell's manual topic, (help :agentstatus-index), and its one-line summary in every request. What was left out: plugin.json and mcp.json as manifests, which the cell contract replaces with a section and a declaration; the skill as a separate file, because a manual topic is what the model reads while the cell runs; and a generic MCP client, because the shipped mcp cell already owns a user's own server list and this cell is a client of the index alone. Nothing of the original is vendored: there was no code to vendor.
